      "name": "Obsidian-EOD-Daily-Log-2330",
      "prompt": "You are the System Architect. It is 23:30 (End of Day). \nGenerate a comprehensive technical audit and daily log for Obsidian.\n\n1. DATA COLLECTION:\n   - Use session_search to review today's high-level architectural decisions and user requests.\n   - Scan `~/.hermes/cron/output/` and specifically the logs of `taiex_orchestrator.py`, `stock_monitor.py`, and `run_night_report.py`.\n\n2. LOG CONTENT REQUIREMENTS:\n   - ## \ud83d\udce5 [Summary] What was done\n     - List technical implementations and configuration changes.\n   - ## \ud83d\udd0d [Analysis] What happened\n     - Factural report of system events (e.g., yfinance errors, data latency, successful downloads).\n     - Include errors encountered and their root causes.\n   - ## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f [Improvement] How it was improved\n     - Specific solutions applied (e.g., pivoting to NQ=F, clearing caches, implementing cross-checkers).\n   - ## \ud83d\udcca [Communication Stats]\n     - List each chat group/target (e.g. 'Home', '\u9ad8\u6f6e\u4e0d\u65b7').\n     - Total count of messages sent to each today.\n     - Identify which automated scripts were the primary senders.\n\n3. STRUCTURE for Obsidian:\n   - YAML Frontmatter (tags: #daily-log #system-audit, date: YYYY-MM-DD).\n   - Use [[Wikilinks]] for linked system components.\n\n4. OUTPUT: Save as `~/Documents/Obsidian Vault/Daily Logs/YYYY-MM-DD.md` and report the path.",
